WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.213 --> 00:00:01.699
- I'm just imagining a big bowl

00:00:01.699 --> 00:00:03.328
of scrambled eggs with bourbon in it.

00:00:03.328 --> 00:00:08.070
("Jingle Bells")

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.550
- I've seen eggnog in movies,

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.002
but I've never seen it in real life.

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:13.300
- I think it's something
that you drink at Christmas

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.673
when you wanna get drunk and
forget about your family.

00:00:15.673 --> 00:00:17.776
- All I know is that it's drunk
during the festive season,

00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:20.282
so Christmas and the
weeks leading up to it.

00:00:20.282 --> 00:00:21.997
- I can't tell if it's good or not

00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:23.158
because when you see it in movies,

00:00:23.158 --> 00:00:25.444
they either love it or
they really hate it.

00:00:25.444 --> 00:00:27.182
- We don't really get a
white Christmas in Australia,

00:00:27.182 --> 00:00:30.678
so this is probably the closest
thing that we're gonna get.

00:00:30.678 --> 00:00:32.084
- I didn't think it was gonna be warm.

00:00:32.084 --> 00:00:33.308
- I can smell the rum.

00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:35.737
- It kinda smells like a dirty eggcup

00:00:35.737 --> 00:00:38.067
has been left in the
dishwasher for two weeks.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.146
- [Voiceover] It actually
looks like dishwater too.

00:00:40.146 --> 00:00:41.232
- It sort of smells like

00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:43.148
somebody's thrown up Christmas pudding.

00:00:43.148 --> 00:00:44.983
- 'Tis the season to be drunk, my friend.

00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:46.579
- Mmm.
(cups clanking)

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.195
- Mmm, that's quite something. (laughs)

00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:49.629
- [Woman] That's good.
- [Man] Yeah.

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:52.713
- It's kinda like a glass
of milk with rum in it.

00:00:52.713 --> 00:00:54.172
- It kinda burns going down,

00:00:54.172 --> 00:00:57.186
so I can see why it's a
good winter Christmas drink.

00:00:57.186 --> 00:00:59.559
- I can already feel it, actually.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.521
It's warming me up and making
me feel a little bit happy.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:05.149
- That tastes like someone spiked custard.

00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:06.060
- It has surprised me.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.257
I can't really taste the egg in it.

00:01:08.257 --> 00:01:10.007
I was really worried it'd be really eggy.

00:01:10.007 --> 00:01:12.484
- It's tricky because Christmas
falls in summer in Australia

00:01:12.484 --> 00:01:14.156
and it does get really hot.

00:01:14.156 --> 00:01:16.815
So, I can't see us drinking
something like this warm.

00:01:16.815 --> 00:01:18.994
- I think maybe we
should try eggnog on ice.

00:01:18.994 --> 00:01:20.235
- Mmm, that would be good.

00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:21.277
That would be good for our Christmas.

00:01:21.277 --> 00:01:22.848
- [Both] Thumbs up, for sure, yeah.

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:23.566
- Bottoms up.

00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:24.442
- Yeah, I could get around it.

00:01:24.442 --> 00:01:26.103
Maybe a Christmas in July thing.

00:01:26.103 --> 00:01:28.217
- Americans know how to do Christmas.

00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.976
They absolutely embrace it and--

00:01:29.976 --> 00:01:33.014
- [Woman] They invented it.
- [Man] Exactly, and eggnog?

00:01:33.014 --> 00:01:34.635
Just another tick on the list.

00:01:34.635 --> 00:01:37.022
- Eggnog sounds like an insult
that you'd call someone,

00:01:37.022 --> 00:01:38.672
like, "You're such an eggnog."

00:01:38.672 --> 00:01:42.007
Yeah, "Oi, your indicator,
you (bleep) eggnog."

00:01:42.007 --> 00:01:43.097
- [Woman] Exactly.
- [Man] Yeah.

